Frozen-phonon check of the 2H-beta soft mode (2026-09-27)

The selected phonopy run (3.5_phonon_dispersion_with_hydrogen_selected/b-Beryllene_bb, PBE+D3, SIGMA 0.1, 13x13 k on 5x5x1)
gives -0.646 THz at the commensurate q = (0.4, 0.6) in the POSCAR reciprocal basis (= (0, 0.4) in the --pa auto basis of
phonopy_disp.yaml). The Gamma-K-M-Gamma band path does not pass through it. The geometry (6.0_dielectric_selection) was relaxed
with PBE without D3, so here the mode is re-tested with the relaxation settings (PBE, no IVDW, SIGMA 0.05).

Supercell: A1 = 5 a1, A2 = a1 + a2 (20 atoms; q . A = 2, 1). k mesh 11 x 65 x 1 (unit-cell 65 x 65 density).
A0: undistorted, A1 / A2: modulation along the soft eigenvector, max |u| = 0.048 / 0.097 A (phonopy amplitude 1 / 2).
E(A) - E(A0) < 0 means the undistorted 2H-beta is unstable against this mode at the PBE level.
